Decisions not in the spec:
- `*` rest is decoded per-segment then joined (so an encoded `%2F` stays data, a literal `/` stays a separator).
- Malformed percent-encoding (`%ZZ`) makes the match fail (`undefined`) instead of throwing, matching the "returns undefined when the path does not match" contract.
- Empty segments from `//` never satisfy `:name`; trailing-slash trimming also covers a bare `*` pattern and `/*`.

